# __PROJECT_NAME__ agent guide

AGENTS.md is a symlink to this file. Keep code, documentation, comments and agent instructions in English.
Read .agents/skills/project/SKILL.md, and the Maximus skill in .agents/skills/maximus/SKILL.md, a link into
node_modules/@arbol-ai/maximus that `bun install` fills.

## Structure

This is a Maximus project on Cloudflare Workers. vite.config.ts is its only configuration: maximus() states
the application and its Worker, and errors.ts, context.ts and auth.ts complete it in code when present.

- routes/: one defineHandler(handler, contract) per file. routes/v1/tasks/[taskId].delete.ts answers
  DELETE /api/v1/tasks/{taskId}; its name, effect and scope derive from the method and path unless declared.
  Declare strict input and output schemas, and MCP or RPC exposure explicitly.
- mcp/tools/: tools only MCP serves, one defineTool per file. mcp/*.md describes the MCP server.
- middleware/: defineMiddleware wraps requests before token admission and sees no principal;
  defineOperationMiddleware runs after admission across HTTP, MCP and RPC.
- pages/: native public Responses at fixed paths. They never contain tenant data.
- src/: optional shared domain code. Root modules never import generated modules or routes.
- tests/: Vitest suites that call `handler` from #maximus/http in Node, signed in with a development token.
- .maximus/: generated by the Vite plugin and `maximus prepare`. Never edit it.

Bindings and triggers belong in maximus() in vite.config.ts; Env is generated from them. Database migrations
and resource creation stay explicit: adding files never provisions infrastructure.

## Boundaries

Tenant authority is the verified principal's organizationId, never caller input. Use the shared Result
pipeline and `fail(code)` for expected failures. Never put credentials, personal or clinical data or request
bodies in logs, examples, errors or agent instructions. Secrets belong in bindings; .dev.vars is local and
ignored. Production tokens are refused until the application configures a real identity provider.

## Workflows

`bun run verify` runs type generation, TypeScript, lint and format, the tests and the build; CI runs it on
every pull request. Use `cf` for Cloudflare: discover commands with `cf cli search` and inspect a command's
schema before running it. Deploy with `bun run deploy` or the GitHub workflow. Preserve unrelated work and
Git identity configuration, and add no assistant attribution to commits.
